{"paper": "2025-Tier1-15-Sep-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "letter-sequence", "splitter": "qn", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 93, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The average height of 15 students is 160 cm. If two students leave, the new average becomes 159 cm. What is the average height of the two students who left?", "options": [{"text": "164.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "166.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "168.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "170.5 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 2, "text": "If P : Q = 5 : 3, Q : R = 4 : 7, and R : S = 2 : 3, find the ratio P : S.", "options": [{"text": "20 : 63", "added": false}, {"text": "40 : 63", "added": false}, {"text": "35 : 72", "added": false}, {"text": "15 : 28", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Simplify: (2.5+ ) − ( × 2.4) 8 4", "options": [{"text": "5.5656", "added": false}, {"text": "6.2225", "added": false}, {"text": "7.0625", "added": false}, {"text": "8.0625", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 4, "text": "Table: Quarterly Revenue. Item Q1 Q2 Q3 Q4 Product A 45 55 50 60 Product B 70 72 68 75 What is the average quarterly revenue of Product B?", "options": [{"text": "Rs. 71.25 lakhs", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 71.5 lakhs", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 72 lakhs", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 72.5 lakhs", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 5, "text": "Simplify: (4 ÷ 7 ) × (3 ÷ 9 )", "options": [{"text": "21/4", "added": false}, {"text": "7/2", "added": false}, {"text": "9/2", "added": false}, {"text": "4/3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A circular disc of radius 6 cm is inscribed in a square. What is the approximate area of the remaining portion of the square?", "options": [{"text": "28.30 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "45.75 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "30.96 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "72.50 cm²", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": "c"}, {"n": 7, "text": "A manufacturer offers a product to a retailer at a 25% discount on the marked price. An additional shipping charge of 8% is applied. The retailer sells for Rs. 2400 more, earning a 35% profit. What was the original marked price?", "options": [{"text": "Rs. 8,465.60", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 9,127.45", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 10,050.76", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 11,254.90", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 8, "text": "How many smaller hemispheres with radius 4 cm can be formed by melting a hemisphere with radius 16 cm?", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 9, "text": "A cone and a hemisphere have the same radius. Their combined height is 24 cm. If both have equal volumes, find the radius.", "options": [{"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "12 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 10, "text": "A trader buys 8 items for the price of 5 items. If he sells each item at a 5% discount on its marked